      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "SHÊN Han-kuang 申涵光 (T. 孚孟, 和孟, H. 鳧盟, 聰山, 臥樗老人), Jan. 4, 1620–1677, July 5, poet, philosopher and artist, was a native of Yung-nien, Chihli. His father, Shên Chia-yin 申佳胤 (T. 孔嘉, 1602–1644), took his own life as a martyr to the Ming cause and was canonized as Tuan-min 端愍 in the Ch'ing period.",
          "source": "eccp-3649403",
          "kind": "source-wording",
          "status": "imported"
        },
        {
